# Editor first

Windows is the majority audience. Those users run the frozen editor as a standalone app (Start Menu, desktop, drop a file on `cleave.exe`). They do not have a terminal. Linux checkout and scripted CLI remain supported; they are not the default product surface.

## New user-facing work

- Design the in-editor path first: overlay, centered modal, or [cleave/viz/loading.py](cleave/viz/loading.py) loading screen. Reuse those, not a native Windows menu bar.
- Share logic in non-viz modules. The editor presents; `cleave.exe <command>` may call the same functions and print to stderr when a console exists.
- Do not ship a feature whose only progress or error channel is stdout/stderr. Explorer, Start Menu, and drop must work with no console.
- Long jobs the editor starts (stem split, weight download, offline render, backup) show named status in the window, plus a progress bar when the work reports bytes or fraction. Failures use a modal or panel notification, not a vanished console.
- CLI-only is fine for CI, `--help` / `--version`, and headless smoke. That does not replace the editor path for the same job.

## Do not

```
# Bad: play on a wav finishes Demucs in the console, then opens the editor
run_separate(wav)   # tqdm / print only
launch(project)

# Good: window first; same run_separate reports into the loading screen
open_window()
run_separate(wav, on_progress=draw_loading)
continue_boot(project)
```
